title: "pocd-hippocampal-power-audit: reproducibility bundle for an animal-level power audit of 3-vs-3 hippocampal single-cell RNA-seq in postoperative neurocognitive dysfunction"
abstract: >-
  Companion code and data for a methodological reanalysis of a published 3-vs-3
  hippocampal single-cell RNA-seq study in a mouse model of postoperative
  neurocognitive dysfunction (GSE267933; 20,684 cells, nine cell types). The
  bundle computes cell-type composition at the level of the animal rather than
  the pooled cell, quantifies how much of the reported significance is produced
  by that choice of inferential unit alone, tests cell state by two independent
  pseudobulk routes (Welch and limma-voom with edgeR TMM), attributes the
  limma-voom hits to ambient RNA, calibrates genome-wide false-positive
  behaviour, and derives the minimum detectable effect and the per-group sample
  size required for a given effect. Every number quoted in the manuscript is
  regenerated by the scripts shipped here.
